{
  "dom_id": "step-q45450",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221743/assets/7625ed8002bbd684ba004185f357e8b8e9b3384857684ef836ccd4a019a317cd.png)\n\nThe stretch $S(x,y)=(\\frac{1}{2}x,\\frac{1}{3}y)$ is applied to the polygon shown above. Which of the following is the resulting polygon?",
  "worked_solution": "To stretch a polygon, we \n\n- find the images of the vertices, and then\n\n- draw segments connecting the image vertices.\n\nSo, our three vertices $(4,6)$, $(5,-3)$, $(-6,-6)$ are mapped to the following points by the stretch:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4,6) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4,\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6)=(2,2) \\\\ (6,-3) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6,\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-3))=(3,-1) \\\\ (-6,-6) & ↦(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-6),\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-6))=(-3,-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following result:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221743/assets/aa9f0b7c785c5c830c0e902f500fe0998df4c4ee8ace07af6989cf9aad2a88ea.png)",
